. Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Lumbar Puncture / CSF Analysis [REPORTED] \u2014 CSF examination to be considered after assessment for safety and contraindications.\n\u2022 Malaria Rapid Antigen / Peripheral Smear [REPORTED] \u2014 Malaria testing sent. Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Dengue NS1 Antigen & Serology [REPORTED] \u2014 Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Serum Electrolytes & Renal Panel [REPORTED] \u2014 Creatinine within normal range. AST and ALT mildly elevated. Blood cultures sent. Malaria testing sent. Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Inflammatory Markers (CRP / ESR) [REPORTED] \u2014 CRP elevated. Creatinine within normal range. AST and ALT mildly elevated. Blood cultures sent. Malaria testing sent. Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Blood & Bacterial Cultures [REPORTED] \u2014 Blood cultures sent. Malaria testing sent. Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Dengue IgM/IgG Serology [ORDERED] \u2014 Pending\n\u2022 Dengue NS1 Antigen and IgM/IgG ELISA [ORDERED] \u2014 Pending", "original_ai_text": "\u2022 Complete Blood Count (CBC) with Differential [REPORTED] \u2014 WBC 8.7 \u00d710\u2079/L, hemoglobin 14.2 g/dL, platelets 138 \u00d710\u2079/L, CRP elevated. Creatinine within normal range. AST and ALT mildly elevated. Blood cultures sent. Malaria testing sent. Dengue testing sent. Further infectious work-up planned according to clinical findings and exposure history.\n\u2022 Lumbar Puncture / CSF Analysis [REPORTED] \u2014 CSF examination to be considered after